\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Quantitative object detection comparison on the KITTI validation set for Bird's-Eye View (BEV) bounding box estimation. Average Precision (AP, \%) is evaluated using 40-point interpolation ($R_{40}$) at Moderate difficulty ($\text  {IoU} \ge 0.70$ for Car; $\text  {IoU} \ge 0.50$ for Pedestrian and Cyclist). The top partition compares compact and real-time BEV/pillar detectors; the bottom partition lists heavier two-stage 3D anchor-based detectors as external reference points. Best values among compact models are in \textbf  {bold}, and second-best values are \underline  {underlined}.}}{16}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
