\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Nine-cell Precision--Recall ($R_{40}$) benchmark curves evaluated under a unified local evaluation harness on the KITTI validation split across Car (left column, $\text  {IoU} \ge 0.70$), Pedestrian (center column, $\text  {IoU} \ge 0.50$), and Cyclist (right column, $\text  {IoU} \ge 0.50$) under Easy (top row), Moderate (middle row), and Hard (bottom row) difficulty regimes. Gold solid curves depict the proposed MobilePIXORNeXt, green dashed curves denote PointPillars, blue dotted curves represent SECOND, and red solid curves denote baseline MobilePIXOR. Shaded areas denote Average Precision integrals. In this unified local benchmark, MobilePIXORNeXt attains $60.75\%$ Moderate AP on Pedestrian, compared to $55.83\%$ for PointPillars and $56.47\%$ for SECOND (versus $56.01\%$ and $56.56\%$ in published reference tables). On Cyclist, SECOND maintains higher Moderate precision ($70.70\%$ local vs. $66.73\%$), while MobilePIXORNeXt improves over PointPillars ($65.86\%$ local).}}{18}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pr_curves}{{8}{18}{Nine-cell Precision--Recall ($R_{40}$) benchmark curves evaluated under a unified local evaluation harness on the KITTI validation split across Car (left column, $\text {IoU} \ge 0.70$), Pedestrian (center column, $\text {IoU} \ge 0.50$), and Cyclist (right column, $\text {IoU} \ge 0.50$) under Easy (top row), Moderate (middle row), and Hard (bottom row) difficulty regimes. Gold solid curves depict the proposed MobilePIXORNeXt, green dashed curves denote PointPillars, blue dotted curves represent SECOND, and red solid curves denote baseline MobilePIXOR. Shaded areas denote Average Precision integrals. In this unified local benchmark, MobilePIXORNeXt attains $60.75\%$ Moderate AP on Pedestrian, compared to $55.83\%$ for PointPillars and $56.47\%$ for SECOND (versus $56.01\%$ and $56.56\%$ in published reference tables). On Cyclist, SECOND maintains higher Moderate precision ($70.70\%$ local vs. $66.73\%$), while MobilePIXORNeXt improves over PointPillars ($65.86\%$ local)}{figure.8}{}}
